 ```
 
+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to format as multiple units, largest first. Hours are the
+largest unit and parts are not separated, so the output is compatible with Go's
+`time.ParseDuration`. Zero parts are skipped, leftover milliseconds are dropped,
+and `long: true` takes precedence.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })      // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+ms(999, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
 ```ts
